0e4deb7c-20e4-44ab-a4a0-51f06dfe54c4-0
00:25:51.200 --> 00:25:57.103
So I just want to quickly talk about what
I think the core pillars of psilocybin

0e4deb7c-20e4-44ab-a4a0-51f06dfe54c4-1
00:25:57.103 --> 00:25:59.800
facilitator training need to include.

0607275f-0341-4f81-99d3-ee064b7bebc9-0
00:26:00.840 --> 00:26:02.760
There's definitely the knowledge, right?

18774b45-2530-4f5c-9260-951e525d853d-0
00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:08.083
We all need to understand the science,
the psychology, what are altered states,

18774b45-2530-4f5c-9260-951e525d853d-1
00:26:08.083 --> 00:26:09.680
what does all that mean?

da6ad06f-91e7-456d-bb93-75a1294eaeab-0
00:26:09.680 --> 00:26:13.656
And not only the science behind it,
the pharmacology,

da6ad06f-91e7-456d-bb93-75a1294eaeab-1
00:26:13.656 --> 00:26:17.560
the also just understanding how this
medicine works.

5afe9df8-9899-4cbe-b38f-72435223a9fd-0
00:26:18.360 --> 00:26:20.040
We also need clinical skills.

ebce5fa8-3b09-4fca-a862-27a79eba9f5c-0
00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:25.664
We need to know what preparation involves,
what is integration and how do we do that,

ebce5fa8-3b09-4fca-a862-27a79eba9f5c-1
00:26:25.664 --> 00:26:30.765
and also how do we facilitate in a way
that it makes the most sense following

ebce5fa8-3b09-4fca-a862-27a79eba9f5c-2
00:26:30.765 --> 00:26:32.400
again the clinical model.

ace409b1-4d2b-4494-b5c5-376bb870822a-0
00:26:33.880 --> 00:26:35.520
Ethics are always important.

146541da-2de1-4947-a29c-b0ec150413bc-0
00:26:36.720 --> 00:26:40.651
It tells us what our boundaries are,
how to keep people safe,

146541da-2de1-4947-a29c-b0ec150413bc-1
00:26:40.651 --> 00:26:42.680
how to do this work responsibly.

bdf5c95f-abae-4ab5-a858-4095a4617c9f-0
00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:48.480
And then I think experiential is also
just as important as the others.

c4f5c70f-0246-4a5d-89e9-7631a397d983-0
00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:55.262
Not only do I feel like everyone needs to
have a relationship with the medicine,

c4f5c70f-0246-4a5d-89e9-7631a397d983-1
00:26:55.262 --> 00:27:01.367
I also think that practicum is a great
way to help people feel confident and

c4f5c70f-0246-4a5d-89e9-7631a397d983-2
00:27:01.367 --> 00:27:06.282
learn how to do this work in a way that
isn't just, you know,

c4f5c70f-0246-4a5d-89e9-7631a397d983-3
00:27:06.282 --> 00:27:12.546
trial and error where people can have
backup and assistance in learning how to

c4f5c70f-0246-4a5d-89e9-7631a397d983-4
00:27:12.546 --> 00:27:15.480
do this work and just really quickly.

7230c076-d0df-4f0a-b0c9-c0842fde2ce1-0
00:27:15.640 --> 00:27:19.955
So if we follow all four of these pillars,
the focus and the hope is that we have

7230c076-d0df-4f0a-b0c9-c0842fde2ce1-1
00:27:19.955 --> 00:27:21.640
safe and effective facilitation.

72b0eb4e-8c95-4407-892d-3317a637aaa6-0
00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:29.596
So now before I go any further,
I do want to talk about this model that

72b0eb4e-8c95-4407-892d-3317a637aaa6-1
00:27:29.596 --> 00:27:35.682
Pata has put together that I think is
really important for us to discuss and to

72b0eb4e-8c95-4407-892d-3317a637aaa6-2
00:27:35.682 --> 00:27:37.279
become more aware of.

0f532d7b-1b75-4bbb-af1e-0898f0ba9bf9-0
00:27:37.280 --> 00:27:43.360
I think we tend as a group to just kind
of lump preparation and integration all

0f532d7b-1b75-4bbb-af1e-0898f0ba9bf9-1
00:27:43.360 --> 00:27:44.120
in as one.

c5f7912d-8788-4c14-bc92-5aea71193695-0
00:27:44.120 --> 00:27:51.218
But really there's there's areas in which
we have both therapeutic and we have

c5f7912d-8788-4c14-bc92-5aea71193695-1
00:27:51.218 --> 00:27:56.160
administrative preparation as well As for
integration.

e08ee29a-1ab2-4936-949a-f8c32b2666bd-0
00:27:56.480 --> 00:28:01.649
So administration is obviously kind of
focusing on logistics, safety, compliance,

e08ee29a-1ab2-4936-949a-f8c32b2666bd-1
00:28:01.649 --> 00:28:04.485
where therapeutic is more the
psychological,

e08ee29a-1ab2-4936-949a-f8c32b2666bd-2
00:28:04.485 --> 00:28:06.440
emotional and clinical process.

8cebf3d0-cf14-4302-9d5e-63d52c1da872-0
00:28:08.800 --> 00:28:12.560
In Oregon,
they're not allowed to actually use

8cebf3d0-cf14-4302-9d5e-63d52c1da872-1
00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:13.200
therapy.

feaa0daa-8894-4909-ba1a-2ae8f1644785-0
00:28:13.560 --> 00:28:16.963
They're,
even though it's called a therapy program,

feaa0daa-8894-4909-ba1a-2ae8f1644785-1
00:28:16.963 --> 00:28:21.480
there's there's no allowance for
therapeutic techniques of any kind.

5eccff87-b350-4a7f-b51c-4046013d417d-0
00:28:22.120 --> 00:28:28.035
And so that's a big part of why prep and
integration have been separated there

5eccff87-b350-4a7f-b51c-4046013d417d-1
00:28:28.035 --> 00:28:34.176
where there is administrative preparation,
but there's no therapeutic preparation

5eccff87-b350-4a7f-b51c-4046013d417d-2
00:28:34.176 --> 00:28:38.520
unless somebody's going to a counselor or
to a therapist.

388a3d75-1018-4a3d-836e-ab4cf8d0e0b5-0
00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:42.708
So if you go to Oregon,
you receive administration, sorry,

388a3d75-1018-4a3d-836e-ab4cf8d0e0b5-1
00:28:42.708 --> 00:28:46.790
administrative prep,
you get the experience and you get that

388a3d75-1018-4a3d-836e-ab4cf8d0e0b5-2
00:28:46.790 --> 00:28:50.136
integration from an administrative point
of view,

388a3d75-1018-4a3d-836e-ab4cf8d0e0b5-3
00:28:50.136 --> 00:28:55.489
but you're not necessarily getting the
therapy piece that requires like another

388a3d75-1018-4a3d-836e-ab4cf8d0e0b5-4
00:28:55.489 --> 00:28:59.102
level, you know,
and or them seeking additional care,

388a3d75-1018-4a3d-836e-ab4cf8d0e0b5-5
00:28:59.102 --> 00:29:04.054
whether that be some people are are
working with their therapist and then

388a3d75-1018-4a3d-836e-ab4cf8d0e0b5-6
00:29:04.054 --> 00:29:07.200
they're going to Oregon to get the
experience.

22348f51-594c-4859-967f-76c1c5c59abd-0
00:29:07.440 --> 00:29:12.127
And then they have the pillows both
before and after where they're actually

22348f51-594c-4859-967f-76c1c5c59abd-1
00:29:12.127 --> 00:29:15.520
getting the therapeutic experience here
in New Mexico.

daaa7592-6e6b-4ca8-9d1c-cf369a63d4a0-0
00:29:15.520 --> 00:29:22.037
It looks like I haven't really heard
anybody discuss this if they're going to

daaa7592-6e6b-4ca8-9d1c-cf369a63d4a0-1
00:29:22.037 --> 00:29:23.040
be separate.

6ac6ef5d-10cb-4f39-857f-dd991cc35a21-0
00:29:23.040 --> 00:29:27.830
It does sound I've heard a little bit
about offering like peer support guides,

6ac6ef5d-10cb-4f39-857f-dd991cc35a21-1
00:29:27.830 --> 00:29:30.560
etcetera,
to maybe help with the experience.

9e28e183-7e4d-4685-92e7-2ac242dca456-0
00:29:31.480 --> 00:29:35.761
But I think it's important that we're
looking at this path here and

9e28e183-7e4d-4685-92e7-2ac242dca456-1
00:29:35.761 --> 00:29:40.924
understanding that there's two different
kinds of prep and two different kinds of

9e28e183-7e4d-4685-92e7-2ac242dca456-2
00:29:40.924 --> 00:29:41.680
integration.

af7c4738-662b-4c71-b450-a9ffc7294e48-0
00:29:42.320 --> 00:29:46.589
In fact, using this model,
some people who don't want to have

af7c4738-662b-4c71-b450-a9ffc7294e48-1
00:29:46.589 --> 00:29:52.166
anything to do with the experience can
still offer the prep and the integration,

af7c4738-662b-4c71-b450-a9ffc7294e48-2
00:29:52.166 --> 00:29:57.536
while we have people on site that are
actually doing the administrative prep,

af7c4738-662b-4c71-b450-a9ffc7294e48-3
00:29:57.536 --> 00:30:00.359
integration, and of course, facilitating.

6b12502e-3e0c-44c5-a427-0514bd196f3c-0
00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:04.173
So I think it's important that we're
examining this framework and

6b12502e-3e0c-44c5-a427-0514bd196f3c-1
00:30:04.173 --> 00:30:06.120
understanding what the differences are.

7da6d402-739d-4671-8d28-fdc0cdb02833-0
00:30:07.040 --> 00:30:11.043
I've been attending the other
subcommittees and I know they're talking

7da6d402-739d-4671-8d28-fdc0cdb02833-1
00:30:11.043 --> 00:30:15.215
already about how many sessions are going
to be required for preparation,

7da6d402-739d-4671-8d28-fdc0cdb02833-2
00:30:15.215 --> 00:30:19.783
but I'm not really seeing the definitions
or the teasing out between therapeutic

7da6d402-739d-4671-8d28-fdc0cdb02833-3
00:30:19.783 --> 00:30:22.433
preparation versus administrative
preparation,

7da6d402-739d-4671-8d28-fdc0cdb02833-4
00:30:22.433 --> 00:30:25.760
being that we're doing a medical model
here in New Mexico.

764cbbd1-7c30-439b-9075-5f41ed96264f-0
00:30:26.640 --> 00:30:29.400
Therapeutic prep and integration is
important.

8e1e8138-6e9a-46ac-a711-efc1bebee9a6-0
00:30:29.400 --> 00:30:34.315
And I from what I understand that is to
be included in this program,

8e1e8138-6e9a-46ac-a711-efc1bebee9a6-1
00:30:34.315 --> 00:30:39.872
but I do think it's really important that
we're understanding that, you know,

8e1e8138-6e9a-46ac-a711-efc1bebee9a6-2
00:30:39.872 --> 00:30:43.720
there's different levels at which people
can operate.

66642827-d776-4589-94be-20d311112504-0
00:30:43.720 --> 00:30:47.041
So if somebody doesn't want to become a
counselor,

66642827-d776-4589-94be-20d311112504-1
00:30:47.041 --> 00:30:51.535
they can still participate by being a
part of the experience and the

66642827-d776-4589-94be-20d311112504-2
00:30:51.535 --> 00:30:53.880
administrative prep and integration.

85b12a90-07ba-4f40-9979-0ecc3912acc0-0
00:30:54.160 --> 00:30:56.600
So I just wanted to like kind of point
that out.

8074bee7-953a-4da8-92b6-6c11e5d966f0-0
00:30:57.480 --> 00:31:02.386
I've also got a couple of slides here
that just distinguish what the difference

8074bee7-953a-4da8-92b6-6c11e5d966f0-1
00:31:02.386 --> 00:31:06.680
is between administrative preparation and
therapeutic preparation is.

818ee297-8e1a-498c-87db-bad890687191-0
00:31:06.680 --> 00:31:10.860
So for administrative,
we're talking about documentation,

818ee297-8e1a-498c-87db-bad890687191-1
00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:15.256
informed consent,
medical review and assessment, scheduling,

818ee297-8e1a-498c-87db-bad890687191-2
00:31:15.256 --> 00:31:18.787
reviewing of policies, procedures,
expectations,

818ee297-8e1a-498c-87db-bad890687191-3
00:31:18.787 --> 00:31:23.400
as well as setting up the environment and
having a safety plan.

e7029048-5522-4a10-a56a-5234add91ded-0
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:30.242
Therapeutic preparation is more about
developing trust and the rapport in

e7029048-5522-4a10-a56a-5234add91ded-1
00:31:30.242 --> 00:31:34.066
setting your intentions,
exploring history, themes,

e7029048-5522-4a10-a56a-5234add91ded-2
00:31:34.066 --> 00:31:40.317
goals of this process, and then of course,
preparing for emotional and psychological

e7029048-5522-4a10-a56a-5234add91ded-3
00:31:40.317 --> 00:31:41.200
experiences.

362cae41-6d9a-4ed7-a3b3-f6ec3c4b5220-0
00:31:42.160 --> 00:31:45.526
A big part of this,
which I believe I'll talk about later, is,

362cae41-6d9a-4ed7-a3b3-f6ec3c4b5220-1
00:31:45.526 --> 00:31:48.145
you know,
how ready are they psychologically for

362cae41-6d9a-4ed7-a3b3-f6ec3c4b5220-2
00:31:48.145 --> 00:31:49.000
this experience?

ffe919e3-1080-4ce8-b2b1-0b9d379f80fe-0
00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:52.590
They might be ready administratively,
like they might like, OK,

ffe919e3-1080-4ce8-b2b1-0b9d379f80fe-1
00:31:52.590 --> 00:31:57.359
I made the time and I'm willing, you know,
I've got the schedule and I'm going to do

ffe919e3-1080-4ce8-b2b1-0b9d379f80fe-2
00:31:57.359 --> 00:31:57.640
this.

79a468a0-ae3b-4902-b5c4-61b551ae5e2e-0
00:31:57.640 --> 00:32:02.840
But are they really ready for this
experience psychologically, emotionally?

57444ac9-f591-4bc9-831c-102e5f495c91-0
00:32:03.080 --> 00:32:06.638
These are things that I think as the,
you know,

57444ac9-f591-4bc9-831c-102e5f495c91-1
00:32:06.638 --> 00:32:12.495
maybe in the counselor point of view
where the practitioners will be utilizing

57444ac9-f591-4bc9-831c-102e5f495c91-2
00:32:12.495 --> 00:32:17.239
the therapeutic preparation to determine
these types of things.

79b53fd8-96d3-469f-91b7-2ca93ffe0467-0
00:32:19.040 --> 00:32:24.061
And with respect to integration,
the administrative aspects include,

79b53fd8-96d3-469f-91b7-2ca93ffe0467-1
00:32:24.061 --> 00:32:29.737
you know, again, scheduling documentation,
coordinating with other providers,

79b53fd8-96d3-469f-91b7-2ca93ffe0467-2
00:32:29.737 --> 00:32:34.903
making sure that they have the
appropriate supports or their matrix is

79b53fd8-96d3-469f-91b7-2ca93ffe0467-3
00:32:34.903 --> 00:32:37.960
sufficient and in place tracking outcomes.

82879975-4bae-40ec-927d-0a51fc6067af-0
00:32:38.360 --> 00:32:43.937
I know that the research subcommittee is
doing a lot of work on collecting data

82879975-4bae-40ec-927d-0a51fc6067af-1
00:32:43.937 --> 00:32:48.400
that would all be, you know,
under the administrative umbrella.

859674b6-abdb-492b-92ce-8ee283305fdd-0
00:32:49.200 --> 00:32:53.240
But then therapeutically,
it's more about processing insights.

b223f9ab-0e21-44db-aacc-e5540823a446-0
00:32:53.800 --> 00:32:57.525
What, what are the, you know,
what are some new patterns and new

b223f9ab-0e21-44db-aacc-e5540823a446-1
00:32:57.525 --> 00:32:59.360
perspectives that are coming up?

5457fe06-c268-464a-a494-abf21ae578d6-0
00:33:00.120 --> 00:33:03.493
How do you actually apply those into
behavioral change,

5457fe06-c268-464a-a494-abf21ae578d6-1
00:33:03.493 --> 00:33:08.251
making sure that they have continued
psychological support around their growth

5457fe06-c268-464a-a494-abf21ae578d6-2
00:33:08.251 --> 00:33:12.046
and around the changes that are happening,
and then of course,

5457fe06-c268-464a-a494-abf21ae578d6-3
00:33:12.046 --> 00:33:15.480
reinforcing self-awareness and these new
understandings.

8b7e1ab5-4be9-44d6-b6c8-b414e867554e-0
00:33:18.800 --> 00:33:23.040
So now I'm going to focus a little bit on
how I deliver my trainings.

71b0d05c-4302-46e2-8100-33f2ae5a5915-0
00:33:23.360 --> 00:33:26.339
I do a didactic instruction for the first
day,

71b0d05c-4302-46e2-8100-33f2ae5a5915-1
00:33:26.339 --> 00:33:30.840
and then on the second day there's an
experiential learning component.

d6ef0bc0-4d12-424f-a648-36c0ea2551f6-0
00:33:32.040 --> 00:33:36.832
And so for the didactic portion,
I am focusing on the science,

d6ef0bc0-4d12-424f-a648-36c0ea2551f6-1
00:33:36.832 --> 00:33:41.016
the pharmacology, the legal,
what are the regulations,

d6ef0bc0-4d12-424f-a648-36c0ea2551f6-2
00:33:41.016 --> 00:33:45.199
what are the contraindications and what
are the risks.

a142b828-19db-43d2-8f8a-47546bba2c14-0
00:33:45.720 --> 00:33:50.600
We talk about clinical skill development,
you know, how do you prepare clients?

8ae7cca3-127d-47e4-ad57-221e6cbd2c16-0
00:33:50.600 --> 00:33:51.760
How do you screen them?

9a4e81ec-912a-4bda-bbc9-b39e51ab8a30-0
00:33:52.800 --> 00:33:55.600
What does non directive facilitation mean?

a490cd10-f8de-4626-bda9-7d21dcd7dc3c-0
00:33:55.800 --> 00:33:58.080
And then how to help people integrate.

33ac7524-7f49-480e-801d-d15a10970647-0
00:33:59.440 --> 00:34:03.931
The second day of my training is an
experiential where half the people choose

33ac7524-7f49-480e-801d-d15a10970647-1
00:34:03.931 --> 00:34:06.120
to dose and half will choose to guide.

7b560ced-515b-4e9a-86f7-565aceb99224-0
00:34:06.560 --> 00:34:11.560
And this will allow participants to have
their own experience in a Safeway.

14c23a12-995c-4039-b858-e33e39864425-0
00:34:11.880 --> 00:34:14.906
Some people want to experience this
medicine,

14c23a12-995c-4039-b858-e33e39864425-1
00:34:14.906 --> 00:34:20.169
and I think it's important that you do
experience the medicine prior to guiding

14c23a12-995c-4039-b858-e33e39864425-2
00:34:20.169 --> 00:34:23.920
clients to fully understand this,
what this medicine is.

c2486a93-16da-4d4a-a831-b348f87b1520-0
00:34:23.920 --> 00:34:27.722
I mean, here's the thing, you know,
for a doctor,

c2486a93-16da-4d4a-a831-b348f87b1520-1
00:34:27.722 --> 00:34:33.654
you don't really have to have had cancer
to understand how chemo works and to

c2486a93-16da-4d4a-a831-b348f87b1520-2
00:34:33.654 --> 00:34:35.480
offer chemo to a client.

8cc62e47-fb3e-4537-aaa6-bb950fe0e975-0
00:34:36.720 --> 00:34:39.240
You can still do the same thing with
psilocybin.

6d3716af-fcba-4663-ae7f-8b164e69c2dc-0
00:34:39.280 --> 00:34:43.163
But I will tell you that if you
understand this medicine personally,

6d3716af-fcba-4663-ae7f-8b164e69c2dc-1
00:34:43.163 --> 00:34:47.159
it's going to make you much,
much better at the work you're doing with

6d3716af-fcba-4663-ae7f-8b164e69c2dc-2
00:34:47.159 --> 00:34:48.960
and helping to guide the client.

59332cb5-c045-46f8-9794-05adfbf5d8cc-0
00:34:50.440 --> 00:34:54.953
And I think that having a place where
people can experience the medicine for

59332cb5-c045-46f8-9794-05adfbf5d8cc-1
00:34:54.953 --> 00:34:56.360
themselves is important.

2e878689-4774-450d-8397-2a21ee843dc8-0
00:34:56.680 --> 00:34:59.385
And I do believe when I talk about
practicum later,

2e878689-4774-450d-8397-2a21ee843dc8-1
00:34:59.385 --> 00:35:03.391
I think this is going to be an important
part of what we need to be offering

2e878689-4774-450d-8397-2a21ee843dc8-2
00:35:03.391 --> 00:35:04.119
practitioners.

001beb51-2eef-4dd5-be4f-2f9758f8d335-0
00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:09.932
It's also on the second day,
I'm offering people a supervised

001beb51-2eef-4dd5-be4f-2f9758f8d335-1
00:35:09.932 --> 00:35:12.240
experience of guiding others.

8f577835-3cca-4c86-ae00-5e18167c1b9d-0
00:35:12.800 --> 00:35:15.120
What does that look like and feel like
and how?

2d471efa-315d-46d9-98a2-46cacc72223e-0
00:35:15.160 --> 00:35:18.503
And then they get to do it,
but knowing they have backup and knowing

2d471efa-315d-46d9-98a2-46cacc72223e-1
00:35:18.503 --> 00:35:20.200
they're not doing it by themselves.

97e54d88-a2cb-4187-bafd-0b077923203d-0
00:35:20.720 --> 00:35:23.920
Also being able to observe multiple
client sessions.

a0e84eea-701a-4d9a-992d-e3e3c905eff7-0
00:35:23.920 --> 00:35:30.165
So when we, when I have my second day,
I might have like 3P3 practitioners are

a0e84eea-701a-4d9a-992d-e3e3c905eff7-1
00:35:30.165 --> 00:35:34.040
dosing and then we may have four or five
guides.

c288779c-be23-44e4-a527-26f4575e10f1-0
00:35:34.400 --> 00:35:39.109
So now we get to experience multiple
different experiences because No2

c288779c-be23-44e4-a527-26f4575e10f1-1
00:35:39.109 --> 00:35:42.160
psilocybin journeys for anybody are the
same.

35d12476-e74d-4062-bee4-dc1feb8aa54f-0
00:35:42.760 --> 00:35:49.111
It's good to have, you know,
different examples to experience so that

35d12476-e74d-4062-bee4-dc1feb8aa54f-1
00:35:49.111 --> 00:35:52.560
it can build confidence and expertise.

9f9a3aef-4d3d-4862-9b08-bfa662d31ea6-0
00:35:53.720 --> 00:35:56.900
And then of course,
I always offer an online integration

9f9a3aef-4d3d-4862-9b08-bfa662d31ea6-1
00:35:56.900 --> 00:35:57.960
after the training.

528edf93-eedb-49e2-9e38-c218bc1fe433-0
00:35:57.960 --> 00:36:03.322
So whoever dosed gets integration,
that's a key and important part of the

528edf93-eedb-49e2-9e38-c218bc1fe433-1
00:36:03.322 --> 00:36:04.120
experience.

0a2a1bb7-12e8-4297-a9b3-e70bdaec51e5-0
00:36:04.520 --> 00:36:08.178
And I, you know,
usually they allow the other class

0a2a1bb7-12e8-4297-a9b3-e70bdaec51e5-1
00:36:08.178 --> 00:36:13.244
members to attend that integration so
that they can also get first hand

0a2a1bb7-12e8-4297-a9b3-e70bdaec51e5-2
00:36:13.244 --> 00:36:16.200
experience on what integration looks like.

3f50e560-2f97-43e9-ac49-04c5d83c89f8-0
00:36:18.720 --> 00:36:22.400
So just a little bit more on the content
that I include.

a004c580-bdc1-466e-9470-c90355ff1ae6-0
00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:26.835
I think it's important that we're talking
about the history and the cultural

a004c580-bdc1-466e-9470-c90355ff1ae6-1
00:36:26.835 --> 00:36:28.120
context of this medicine.

25c6a2d4-16a6-4c6f-93af-aad1e19c409b-0
00:36:28.720 --> 00:36:33.520
The difference, you know,
between clinical and ceremonial use.

1e152904-5312-4bac-8756-0eb60ba23d0e-0
00:36:34.240 --> 00:36:40.465
What the history has shown around the
suppression of research and how research

1e152904-5312-4bac-8756-0eb60ba23d0e-1
00:36:40.465 --> 00:36:44.800
has emerged again,
and so grateful for that happening.

e4e0859c-dded-4aa4-8e28-826bd6dabb66-0
00:36:45.320 --> 00:36:49.142
And then of course,
it's important to understand and be aware

e4e0859c-dded-4aa4-8e28-826bd6dabb66-1
00:36:49.142 --> 00:36:52.040
of ethics around traditional medicine
origins.

57f0e59c-f0a6-4e01-988a-96f4af075409-0
00:36:53.200 --> 00:36:57.012
Then of course,
moving on to the science and pharmacology,

57f0e59c-f0a6-4e01-988a-96f4af075409-1
00:36:57.012 --> 00:36:59.920
I make sure people understand what you
know.

05e3406b-e86b-4225-bc2f-71bc560f35da-0
00:36:59.920 --> 00:37:04.678
They know what psilocybin is,
how it interacts with the serotonin

05e3406b-e86b-4225-bc2f-71bc560f35da-1
00:37:04.678 --> 00:37:07.922
receptors,
what is the default mode network,

05e3406b-e86b-4225-bc2f-71bc560f35da-2
00:37:07.922 --> 00:37:12.319
what is ego dissolution and how that
impacts the experience.

b2991bbb-33cb-46e6-b88d-9d22edae7756-0
00:37:13.440 --> 00:37:18.365
Although I focus on dosing ranges and the
pharmakinetics around that,

b2991bbb-33cb-46e6-b88d-9d22edae7756-1
00:37:18.365 --> 00:37:22.164
I also talk about the legal and
regulatory landscape,

b2991bbb-33cb-46e6-b88d-9d22edae7756-2
00:37:22.164 --> 00:37:26.526
that it is a federal,
federally scheduled one drug that a lot

b2991bbb-33cb-46e6-b88d-9d22edae7756-3
00:37:26.526 --> 00:37:31.873
of states are trying to decriminalize or
implement these types of regulated

b2991bbb-33cb-46e6-b88d-9d22edae7756-4
00:37:31.873 --> 00:37:37.080
programs and what the responsibilities
are within the medical frameworks.

e6d9c7bd-9a6f-47ee-b371-bb66f901e6e0-0
00:37:39.480 --> 00:37:43.609
I also make sure to take time to talk
about risk awareness and participant

e6d9c7bd-9a6f-47ee-b371-bb66f901e6e0-1
00:37:43.609 --> 00:37:44.160
screening.

a7ddce60-e8fd-48ed-bd75-c07dd04eff92-0
00:37:45.080 --> 00:37:48.480
Not everybody is going to be well suited
for this experience.

a22a4fbe-bcdb-410e-a67a-8678df8533ac-0
