happens, let me know.

f23dbb56-93e9-4084-bb03-2d50573cd00c-0
00:46:28.760 --> 00:46:32.634
We will, you know,
we'll probably have you switch positions,

f23dbb56-93e9-4084-bb03-2d50573cd00c-1
00:46:32.634 --> 00:46:37.462
switch the song, go to the restroom,
do something and then I will feed them

f23dbb56-93e9-4084-bb03-2d50573cd00c-2
00:46:37.462 --> 00:46:40.320
one of their intentions that they,
you know,

f23dbb56-93e9-4084-bb03-2d50573cd00c-3
00:46:40.320 --> 00:46:43.623
that they prepared and that will then
take them in,

f23dbb56-93e9-4084-bb03-2d50573cd00c-4
00:46:43.623 --> 00:46:45.720
back in in a different direction.

33cc899d-dd3e-4fd7-811e-703fda82200b-0
00:46:46.600 --> 00:46:53.523
I have found that using these intentions
is also been the best way to assess the

33cc899d-dd3e-4fd7-811e-703fda82200b-1
00:46:53.523 --> 00:46:56.600
experience in the integration phase.

62085c80-6a1d-4dc5-9506-db3cf10a6c7e-0
00:46:58.080 --> 00:47:02.128
In the beginning of doing this work,
a lot of people would come to me and say,

62085c80-6a1d-4dc5-9506-db3cf10a6c7e-1
00:47:02.128 --> 00:47:04.178
well,
my intention is to be open to the

62085c80-6a1d-4dc5-9506-db3cf10a6c7e-2
00:47:04.178 --> 00:47:04.640
medicine.

2196fc13-c271-4264-9cef-3da2a1885e15-0
00:47:06.200 --> 00:47:07.800
And I thought, wow, that's great.

ffed2cdf-0576-45fe-8848-53e5c1bd6c82-0
00:47:08.480 --> 00:47:12.246
But what I've learned is, yeah,
I think everyone needs to have that

ffed2cdf-0576-45fe-8848-53e5c1bd6c82-1
00:47:12.246 --> 00:47:12.800
intention.

6e862e20-1a5c-420c-81eb-066bc370fd2a-0
00:47:12.800 --> 00:47:14.360
Like that should already be an attention.

5b42acd1-c564-4fcf-936f-460b0f024920-0
00:47:14.360 --> 00:47:17.150
If it's not an intention,
then they're not ready for this

5b42acd1-c564-4fcf-936f-460b0f024920-1
00:47:17.150 --> 00:47:17.680
experience.

a995a110-a542-4f8b-92b8-c2aef7810ff6-0
00:47:18.160 --> 00:47:19.760
That's part of being ready.

003df2f9-6f62-4021-ae86-efb6aeafec5b-0
00:47:21.360 --> 00:47:25.636
I have found that when people just have
that as their intention,

003df2f9-6f62-4021-ae86-efb6aeafec5b-1
00:47:25.636 --> 00:47:29.320
they come through it going, yeah, OK,
I got some stuff.

67da6ce8-d8d2-4be0-a30e-82394371be01-0
00:47:29.920 --> 00:47:35.786
But they're not able to actually see the
profound implications of the experience

67da6ce8-d8d2-4be0-a30e-82394371be01-1
00:47:35.786 --> 00:47:40.928
as well as if they had a list of
intentions that we can now go through

67da6ce8-d8d2-4be0-a30e-82394371be01-2
00:47:40.928 --> 00:47:44.840
with them and they can see the shifts for
themselves.

96fdef2b-0478-49e3-a162-e3b10b637bbf-0
00:47:45.320 --> 00:47:48.530
And I'm going to tell you that nine times
out of 10,

96fdef2b-0478-49e3-a162-e3b10b637bbf-1
00:47:48.530 --> 00:47:53.316
people come through and 90% of their list
has been addressed or no longer is a

96fdef2b-0478-49e3-a162-e3b10b637bbf-2
00:47:53.316 --> 00:47:53.680
thing.

4d917070-2af3-47fa-800a-7d9104dfd192-0
00:47:54.360 --> 00:47:56.640
I find that intentions are critical.

eb3d9fb5-1ee9-4d76-86c1-9bfcd7f4dfae-0
00:47:57.600 --> 00:48:02.484
So intentions provide direction without
imposing control on the experience

eb3d9fb5-1ee9-4d76-86c1-9bfcd7f4dfae-1
00:48:02.484 --> 00:48:04.960
because they created those intentions.

aa41282f-cd1d-4f0e-9e04-9371e0ca1d7a-0
00:48:04.960 --> 00:48:09.965
I may have helped them formulate them,
but they are their intentions and we're

aa41282f-cd1d-4f0e-9e04-9371e0ca1d7a-1
00:48:09.965 --> 00:48:12.120
using the words that they provide.

a7d3a28c-99bb-422d-af06-c81a9036862d-0
00:48:12.400 --> 00:48:14.200
I don't change the wording.

130ec574-7549-45e6-be7b-6d02b7799e65-0
00:48:14.200 --> 00:48:19.880
I literally read it exactly as is to help
them focus on their experience.

c53fb38a-25c5-4132-8729-913d20cc6a57-0
00:48:20.280 --> 00:48:23.596
Without intentions,
they may have an amazing experience,

c53fb38a-25c5-4132-8729-913d20cc6a57-1
00:48:23.596 --> 00:48:27.320
very much like an Alice in Wonderland
going down a rabbit hole.

bfc6b5b8-7698-411f-801d-bf0f72165414-0
00:48:27.760 --> 00:48:31.370
With intentions,
I'm I know they're going to work on the

bfc6b5b8-7698-411f-801d-bf0f72165414-1
00:48:31.370 --> 00:48:36.310
things they want to work on and the
therapeutic outcomes will be dramatically

bfc6b5b8-7698-411f-801d-bf0f72165414-2
00:48:36.310 --> 00:48:37.640
improved as a result.

7b315b88-2577-4271-9043-0231ce38f0de-0
00:48:40.400 --> 00:48:46.320
It's also important to teach people how
to manage challenging experiences.

d90e1296-db37-47f3-a5e1-545fb8fcc9b0-0
00:48:46.880 --> 00:48:52.257
You know when it's not uncommon for
people to be experiencing anxiety, fear,

d90e1296-db37-47f3-a5e1-545fb8fcc9b0-1
00:48:52.257 --> 00:48:55.680
or panic,
especially during the induction phase.

7e178c6e-52b6-490b-969b-c24b186ed108-0
00:48:56.640 --> 00:49:00.071
It can also be that they're having to
relive something in order to work through

7e178c6e-52b6-490b-969b-c24b186ed108-1
00:49:00.071 --> 00:49:00.200
it.

ffd2a52c-f847-4cd6-ae1a-7f80807f0598-0
00:49:01.680 --> 00:49:07.120
Emotional release and trauma activation
are are are definitely possible.

c5dd30a1-28ff-4496-b233-832cfea739df-0
00:49:07.560 --> 00:49:10.280
People can be confused and disoriented as
well.

96a2e803-d5f7-4d8e-8cd8-100e05067566-0
00:49:10.840 --> 00:49:16.616
So it's important that facilitators know
like when to to have them lean in to what

96a2e803-d5f7-4d8e-8cd8-100e05067566-1
00:49:16.616 --> 00:49:21.279
they're experiencing versus when are we
going to try to, you know,

96a2e803-d5f7-4d8e-8cd8-100e05067566-2
00:49:21.279 --> 00:49:26.359
help them kind of come out and then go
back in in a different direction.

dc4a86fc-3e4a-40ba-b747-044c05e96c17-0
00:49:27.320 --> 00:49:31.463
It's also really important as
facilitators that we maintain a calm,

dc4a86fc-3e4a-40ba-b747-044c05e96c17-1
00:49:31.463 --> 00:49:32.560
grounded presence.

c8e135f6-5a81-428e-8500-2366ef2ddc2b-0
00:49:33.480 --> 00:49:38.126
I've seen it over and over again where
practitioners get very uncomfortable when

c8e135f6-5a81-428e-8500-2366ef2ddc2b-1
00:49:38.126 --> 00:49:42.256
somebody starts to emote and it's,
or even if they're getting angry and

c8e135f6-5a81-428e-8500-2366ef2ddc2b-2
00:49:42.256 --> 00:49:46.960
they're starting to release, you know,
maybe they're, they're starting to scream.

a8975dc5-d75d-4927-b8bc-2913c6f347f5-0
00:49:49.200 --> 00:49:53.381
It's important to help people feel
comfortable that this is part of their

a8975dc5-d75d-4927-b8bc-2913c6f347f5-1
00:49:53.381 --> 00:49:58.014
process that they need to go through and
providing reassurance and orientation to

a8975dc5-d75d-4927-b8bc-2913c6f347f5-2
00:49:58.014 --> 00:50:02.026
the client to help them focus on the
things that they want to focus on

a8975dc5-d75d-4927-b8bc-2913c6f347f5-3
00:50:02.026 --> 00:50:06.547
supporting the participant and staying
with the experience so that they can get

a8975dc5-d75d-4927-b8bc-2913c6f347f5-4
00:50:06.547 --> 00:50:07.960
the therapeutic outcomes.

e500356f-307c-4e9a-a254-b15fd7bc63e2-0
00:50:09.520 --> 00:50:11.680
You know, growth requires.

1e19e388-3cb7-4c5d-9efc-daa52ca28501-0
00:50:12.840 --> 00:50:17.896
It requires us to sometimes go through
challenge and these experiences are not

1e19e388-3cb7-4c5d-9efc-daa52ca28501-1
00:50:17.896 --> 00:50:19.240
always very pleasant.

999647d2-5d5a-4b73-9d87-0880900d51da-0
00:50:19.240 --> 00:50:20.720
Sometimes they are hard.

04ae4a33-fd19-4938-a8ae-f04cc6856d00-0
00:50:21.160 --> 00:50:24.263
But the outcomes,
if you stick with it and you,

04ae4a33-fd19-4938-a8ae-f04cc6856d00-1
00:50:24.263 --> 00:50:28.789
you're providing the safety and the space
they need in the container,

04ae4a33-fd19-4938-a8ae-f04cc6856d00-2
00:50:28.789 --> 00:50:33.573
they can get through it with very,
very positive outcomes having actually

04ae4a33-fd19-4938-a8ae-f04cc6856d00-3
00:50:33.573 --> 00:50:36.160
worked through that trauma or that fear.

11855929-60ed-4d2c-914b-9c4181fa540b-0
00:50:37.280 --> 00:50:39.887
And then of course,
we always want to adjust the environment

11855929-60ed-4d2c-914b-9c4181fa540b-1
00:50:39.887 --> 00:50:40.400
when needed.

b4347e86-a8e7-4f68-a484-796d52ab3faa-0
00:50:40.600 --> 00:50:43.448
It's,
it's not unusual for somebody to say

b4347e86-a8e7-4f68-a484-796d52ab3faa-1
00:50:43.448 --> 00:50:48.218
something about the environment that's
bothering them, the temperature,

b4347e86-a8e7-4f68-a484-796d52ab3faa-2
00:50:48.218 --> 00:50:49.080
the lighting.

78a0d23c-7229-4d8b-a5e4-8c2518bf2a6c-0
00:50:49.920 --> 00:50:53.640
And it's important as facilitators that
we're helping to address that.

9801face-b208-4bde-832d-51549900c6f8-0
00:50:54.720 --> 00:51:00.716
One of the things I do want to say about
the way in which I operate,

9801face-b208-4bde-832d-51549900c6f8-1
00:51:00.716 --> 00:51:07.320
the the way in which I facilitate,
is I tell people that I want them to let

9801face-b208-4bde-832d-51549900c6f8-2
00:51:07.320 --> 00:51:12.795
me take care of them,
lean into the experience and allow me to

9801face-b208-4bde-832d-51549900c6f8-3
00:51:12.795 --> 00:51:14.360
do all the things.

32f20f41-1d2f-4add-8294-f236abf01ed3-0
00:51:14.360 --> 00:51:17.720
If they don't like the song on their
playlist, let me change it for them.

e2fe6cca-a769-4bdf-bde2-3dd08b2bbd1f-0
00:51:18.360 --> 00:51:21.240
If they need more water,
I will go get it for them.

7f4b0172-7104-4758-bda8-4fb331291916-0
00:51:22.080 --> 00:51:25.719
I have had many,
many people after their journeys come to

7f4b0172-7104-4758-bda8-4fb331291916-1
00:51:25.719 --> 00:51:30.739
me and say that the most therapeutic part
of their experience was the fact that

7f4b0172-7104-4758-bda8-4fb331291916-2
00:51:30.739 --> 00:51:35.885
they didn't have to worry about anything
and that there was somebody there caring

7f4b0172-7104-4758-bda8-4fb331291916-3
00:51:35.885 --> 00:51:38.959
for them and taking care of every need
they had.

e623ae9b-8eb5-4615-9841-9b61d24d3b5f-0
00:51:39.200 --> 00:51:41.800
If they need to use the restroom,
I'm going to walk them there.

4bdfcaed-ff4d-400c-927a-7470453e979e-0
00:51:42.200 --> 00:51:45.177
I'm not going to just say, oh,
just give them like direct them to the

4bdfcaed-ff4d-400c-927a-7470453e979e-1
00:51:45.177 --> 00:51:45.560
restroom.

33faf9ab-f93e-4761-828d-cb24234bf6f9-0
00:51:45.560 --> 00:51:47.731
No,
I'm literally going to have them put

33faf9ab-f93e-4761-828d-cb24234bf6f9-1
00:51:47.731 --> 00:51:51.440
their hands on the my shoulders and I'm
walking them to the restroom.

6a65dd04-b131-427d-bc6e-9bce73bfba0b-0
00:51:52.640 --> 00:51:57.275
Many clients have said that having
somebody take care of them teaches them

6a65dd04-b131-427d-bc6e-9bce73bfba0b-1
00:51:57.275 --> 00:52:00.797
to take care of themselves,
especially when they're the,

6a65dd04-b131-427d-bc6e-9bce73bfba0b-2
00:52:00.797 --> 00:52:05.927
they're under the neuroplasticity of the
medicine and they're allowing somebody to

6a65dd04-b131-427d-bc6e-9bce73bfba0b-3
00:52:05.927 --> 00:52:07.040
take care of them.

bb16f02b-1541-4240-9877-658b3691c79c-0
00:52:07.600 --> 00:52:11.677
Chances are when they leave,
they're going to allow others in a little

bb16f02b-1541-4240-9877-658b3691c79c-1
00:52:11.677 --> 00:52:16.157
bit more in helping to take care of
themselves and hopefully they're going to

bb16f02b-1541-4240-9877-658b3691c79c-2
00:52:16.157 --> 00:52:18.800
prioritize taking care of themselves as
well.

e6546b78-767f-417a-b72d-33b5563587e8-0
00:52:21.720 --> 00:52:24.963
Integration is,
is extremely important and it is a,

e6546b78-767f-417a-b72d-33b5563587e8-1
00:52:24.963 --> 00:52:29.453
it's interesting because a lot of people
come to me and they say, well,

e6546b78-767f-417a-b72d-33b5563587e8-2
00:52:29.453 --> 00:52:31.200
what exactly is integration?

26028acb-413d-43a9-89c8-05c764c80641-0
00:52:31.920 --> 00:52:35.160
And integration is essentially
counselling.

be584582-cdf0-432e-a684-07641db84d43-0
00:52:35.960 --> 00:52:40.138
You know,
when we have a client that has an insight,

be584582-cdf0-432e-a684-07641db84d43-1
00:52:40.138 --> 00:52:44.080
we're helping them to apply that into
their life.

ec741dab-a1ee-4257-958b-f22d0be85f2e-0
00:52:44.080 --> 00:52:45.680
That's what we do as counsellors.

072c938b-fe9e-4d4c-8604-d5933e2df05a-0
00:52:45.840 --> 00:52:49.380
Usually they come to counselling because
they're recognizing something big in

072c938b-fe9e-4d4c-8604-d5933e2df05a-1
00:52:49.380 --> 00:52:49.880
their life.

52c3065c-9e82-42e7-8efc-be88fdc39c5c-0
00:52:50.400 --> 00:52:53.511
For example,
I'm realizing that my husband isn't good

52c3065c-9e82-42e7-8efc-be88fdc39c5c-1
00:52:53.511 --> 00:52:57.890
for me and I need to examine this
relationship and see if this is the right

52c3065c-9e82-42e7-8efc-be88fdc39c5c-2
00:52:57.890 --> 00:52:58.640
thing for me.

62970ee5-3332-4945-97c9-aa84e7cbc2f1-0
00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:02.126
Well,
a counselor is there to have allow them

62970ee5-3332-4945-97c9-aa84e7cbc2f1-1
00:53:02.126 --> 00:53:07.428
the safety to explore what they need to
explore to be able to apply these new

62970ee5-3332-4945-97c9-aa84e7cbc2f1-2
00:53:07.428 --> 00:53:09.400
insights that they're having.

fcb8a9e2-8dd1-4abf-9169-a0338cb2bf9e-0
00:53:09.920 --> 00:53:12.924
We're doing the same exact thing with
integration,

fcb8a9e2-8dd1-4abf-9169-a0338cb2bf9e-1
00:53:12.924 --> 00:53:16.400
except the insights happened during the
experience, right?

c41a629d-179c-4bf6-a69e-7ca7e4576e71-0
00:53:16.400 --> 00:53:19.780
They're these big insights where when ego
goes offline,

c41a629d-179c-4bf6-a69e-7ca7e4576e71-1
00:53:19.780 --> 00:53:23.040
we're making connections that we don't
normally make.

f0595814-af80-4379-b22b-6d2d0cdc3a8b-0
00:53:23.680 --> 00:53:29.617
And so it's the role of the facilitator
when it comes to integration is to help

f0595814-af80-4379-b22b-6d2d0cdc3a8b-1
00:53:29.617 --> 00:53:35.258
them to like just to help them reflect on
what's coming up for them without

f0595814-af80-4379-b22b-6d2d0cdc3a8b-2
00:53:35.258 --> 00:53:40.230
imposing our own meaning,
but allowing them to make meaning out of

f0595814-af80-4379-b22b-6d2d0cdc3a8b-3
00:53:40.230 --> 00:53:42.680
what they experienced themselves.

cb0aeaab-3aff-456c-8e47-a7999eba7d98-0
00:53:43.080 --> 00:53:46.555
We're helping to support their emotional
processing,

cb0aeaab-3aff-456c-8e47-a7999eba7d98-1
00:53:46.555 --> 00:53:48.720
translating insights into action.

d75fd3e8-b72f-4085-8ba0-d481e5ef4a75-0
00:53:49.160 --> 00:53:50.520
How do I apply this?

038063e6-de67-4e45-a238-00dbebfe2eed-0
00:53:50.520 --> 00:53:54.036
Now that I understand this new thing
about my mother,

038063e6-de67-4e45-a238-00dbebfe2eed-1
00:53:54.036 --> 00:53:56.120
how do I how do I deal with her?

0d8ea8ac-2c0a-4acb-b854-ac11468ab260-0
00:53:56.120 --> 00:53:57.440
How do I work with her?

f8a1f71e-71be-4562-9ebb-80de8e21cd98-0
00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:04.801
So what are some integration practices,
structured reflection and discussion,

f8a1f71e-71be-4562-9ebb-80de8e21cd98-1
00:54:04.801 --> 00:54:09.480
identifying patterns and new perspectives
and supporting behavioral change.

fbebbcd9-3ca3-4ca5-86ad-02afeb160848-0
00:54:10.160 --> 00:54:11.600
And then there's ongoing support.

54fccd9b-7716-4b1a-ad5a-fb11a701df64-0
00:54:11.720 --> 00:54:14.720
You know, insights can unfold,
unfold over time.

9b214813-d8e4-4d19-9a62-e29859a123e1-0
00:54:15.120 --> 00:54:19.960
I've known people that can have insights
a year after their their journey.

ee6ce045-0dad-43d0-a6db-136d6cda685a-0
00:54:21.520 --> 00:54:24.546
It's because maybe there was a piece of
it that, you know,

ee6ce045-0dad-43d0-a6db-136d6cda685a-1
00:54:24.546 --> 00:54:27.880
not necessarily that they forgot,
but they just didn't focus on.

feca89e1-5583-4c2f-97c7-ffd5f74ee1ff-0
00:54:27.880 --> 00:54:31.560
But then a year later something happens
and Oh my gosh, I understand it now.

f23fe5c8-dee4-4bf2-9c2c-9ad5df6c8bb2-0
00:54:32.080 --> 00:54:37.515
So I think follow up sessions can
reinforce outcomes and having continued

f23fe5c8-dee4-4bf2-9c2c-9ad5df6c8bb2-1
00:54:37.515 --> 00:54:40.600
support improves safety and effectiveness.

5117ab11-4f9b-4700-8ff7-570aa73630a4-0
00:54:40.960 --> 00:54:45.682
I've worked with a client before for a
couple months and then I'll I'll hear

5117ab11-4f9b-4700-8ff7-570aa73630a4-1
00:54:45.682 --> 00:54:50.405
from them like 3 months later because oh,
I have to process a new part of my

5117ab11-4f9b-4700-8ff7-570aa73630a4-2
00:54:50.405 --> 00:54:51.080
experience.

